            <ArticleTitle>Successful repair of intimal dissection following coronary angioplasty with a 48-hour inflation of spiral inflation coil and local delivery of heparin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report on an unusual patient with a threatened occlusive dissection, in whom prolonged (48-hr) inflation of a balloon catheter with localized heparin infusion proved successful. This intracoronary infusion catheter maintained distal coronary flow on a unique spiral coil design, and may provide an alternative or a bridge to emergency operation or stent implantation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
